A simpler way out is just to use %in% rather than ==, as that does do what
people expect.  (%in% is only in S-PLUS 6.1 and R but you can do
equivalent things with is.element in S-PLUS >= 4. The example given in
MASS4 is

painters[is.element(School, c("A", "B", "D")), ]
painters[School %in% c("A", "B", "D"), ]   ## R and S+6.1 only

followed by a warning to consider the effect of NAs.)

