Inference will not be easy for the effect of rx if you use time-dependent 
covariates.  And depending on how you slice the time axis and model the 
interaction between time and rx, the "time-slicing" approach using the coxph 
function will have the same spending of d.f. and increase in variance as the 
continuous time interaction method that is easy to do with SAS PHREG.  Note 
also that you can have continuous time interactions with coxph; it will just 
require the creation of a large dataset.

Frank
