Conversion from RGB to CMYK is not straightforward: the colour spaces have 
non-nested gamuts (and you also need to know exactly what you mean by RGB 
and CMYK, the latter depending on the paper to be used for example, and 
the conventions differ by country).

I would use something like Adobe PhotoShop to convert the EPS file to 
CMYK, and accept that will rasterize.  On the one occasion I had to do 
this (a long time ago) I used such a program to convert the small 
numebr of colours, noted the CMYK colours chosen and hand-edited the 
postscript output to convert to using cmyk operators.

