Herb,

If you are running Splus6.1 for Windows, you should examine the "maps" library. 
 There are functions there that create maps that allow you to hide interior 
boundaries between regions. 

  library(maps)
  help(map)

If you look at the function definition, you can see how they do things.  
Essentially they take advantage of the "duplicated" function to look for shared 
boundaries then drop them out of the map coordinates list so that the region 
becomes one single polygon.

I hope this helps,

Rod

