From P.J.Wells at open.ac.uk  Fri May 16 15:21:57 2003
From: P.J.Wells at open.ac.uk (P.J.Wells)
Date: Fri, 16 May 2003 16:21:57 +0100
Subject: SUMMARY: result of all.equal()
Message-ID: <2AF05AF70A86A6438445BC3AC057F49820317E@mir.open.ac.uk>

I asked whether T and a character string exhausted the possible values
returned by all.equal()

Sam Buttrey pointed out that, strictly speaking, the alternative to T is a
*vector* of character strings.

For those who have S-Plus 6, Chuck Taylor suggested

        message.1 <- if (identical(all.equal(V, V1+V2), TRUE)) "OK" else
"FAIL"

as an alternative to my

        if(is.character(all.equal(V, V1+V2))) message.1 <- "FAIL" else
message.1 <- "OK"
 
I'm still in S+2k, in which

        message.1 <- if (all.equal(V, V1+V2)==T) "OK" else "FAIL"

seems equivalent in effect to Chuck's suggestion.

