Hello,

 

This is a follow-up about my question about 
including time-dependent covariates in coxph() or cph().. Thanks mainly to help 
from prof. Frank Harrell I found the following:

 

1) you need to create an expanded data-set: 
very easy with a function provided in s-news called expand.breakpoints() 
(PS: many thanks to author John Maindonald)

 

2) you need to create the time interaction variable 
before cph() or coxph():

 

    time.rx<-rx*Tstop  # 
Tstop is a variable created by expand.breakpoints()

 

3) use coxph() or cph() :

 

f<-cph(Surv(Tstart,Tstop,status)~age+sex+dm+rx+time.rx,x=T,y=T)

 

this works fine as opposed to 

 

f<-cph(Surv(Tstart,Tstop,status)~age+sex+dm+rx+rx:Tstop,x=T,y=T)

 

will give a singularity error

 

4) Unfortunately validate() calibrate() 
functions which are great functions in Prof. Harrell's  Design 
library no longer work..

 

If any one is aware of a validation and calibration 
method that would work with coxph() with time-dependent covariates please let me 
know..

 

Osman   

 

 

 

  On Sat, 10 May 2003 23:59:40 -0400
Osman Al-Radi <osman.al.radi at utoronto.ca> 
wrote:

